# RunicAI Context Engineering

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"},
  {:runic_ai, path: "~/wrk/runic_ai"}
])

Code.require_file("support/runic_ai_livebook.exs", __DIR__)
```

## What This Notebook Teaches

Context engineering is the practice of deciding what should be visible to the
model for this turn, why it should be visible, and what provenance it carries.

RunicAI separates:

* transcript truth: durable user, assistant, and tool messages
* derived context: summaries, memories, retrieval results, focus, and pressure
* prompt projection: the final provider-facing context

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  transcript[Conversation transcript] --> context_graph[Context graph]
  context_graph --> focus[Focus]
  focus --> memory[Memory recall]
  focus --> retrieval[Retrieval]
  memory --> bundle[Context bundle]
  retrieval --> bundle
  context_graph --> pressure[Window pressure]
  pressure --> compaction[Compaction]
  compaction --> bundle
  bundle --> prompt[Prompt]
```

## Provider Setup

```elixir
setup = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.inputs()
```

```elixir
model = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.read_model!(setup)
llm_opts = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.llm_opts(model, max_output_tokens: RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.read_max_output_tokens(setup))
```

## Build Focus Explicitly

Focus is a contract for what matters now. It should be small enough to reason
about and rich enough to drive memory and retrieval.

```elixir
alias RunicAI.Context.Focus

focus =
  Focus.new!(
    goal: "Help the user debug a production deploy.",
    questions: ["Did assets compile?", "Did migrations run?"],
    entities: ["release", "assets", "database"],
    constraints: ["Keep the answer operational and concise"]
  )

focus
```

## Local Memory And Retrieval Inputs

The recipe can use external stores, but a Livebook is a better place to start
with visible local data.

```elixir
alias RunicAI.Memory.Entry
alias RunicAI.Retrieval.Document

memory_entries = [
  Entry.new!(
    kind: :semantic,
    content: "The user's production app deploys with Docker and runs assets in a release step.",
    summary: "Docker release deploy with asset build step",
    salience: 0.9
  )
]

retrieval_docs = [
  Document.new!(
    id: "deploy-runbook",
    content:
      "When assets are missing after deploy, verify the release image ran npm build and priv/static exists.",
    score: 0.8,
    metadata: %{title: "Deploy runbook"}
  )
]

Kino.Layout.tabs(
  Memory: Kino.DataTable.new(Enum.map(memory_entries, &Map.take(&1, [:kind, :summary, :salience]))),
  Retrieval:
    Kino.DataTable.new(
      Enum.map(retrieval_docs, fn doc ->
        %{id: doc.id, title: doc.metadata.title, score: doc.score}
      end)
    )
)
```

## Visualize The Context-Aware Workflow

```elixir
alias RunicAI.Recipes.SummaryBackedChatAgent

context_workflow =
  SummaryBackedChatAgent.new(
    model: model,
    system: "You are an SRE assistant. Explain only what is supported by context.",
    memory_store: memory_entries,
    retrieval_provider: retrieval_docs,
    llm_opts: llm_opts
  )

RunicAI.Livebook.WorkflowViz.tabs(context_workflow)
```

## Run A Context-Aware Turn

```elixir
RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.require_openai_key!()

context_run =
  context_workflow
  |> Runic.Workflow.react_until_satisfied(%{
    user: "The deploy finished, but the app serves missing CSS. What should I check first?",
    focus: focus
  })

SummaryBackedChatAgent.latest_reply_text(context_run)
```

```elixir
Kino.Layout.tabs(
  Focus: Kino.Tree.new(SummaryBackedChatAgent.latest_focus(context_run)),
  Pressure: Kino.Tree.new(SummaryBackedChatAgent.latest_pressure_decision(context_run)),
  Bundle: Kino.Tree.new(SummaryBackedChatAgent.latest_bundle(context_run)),
  State: Kino.Tree.new(SummaryBackedChatAgent.latest_state(context_run))
)
```

## Interactive Context Chat

```elixir
RunicAI.Livebook.Chat.start(
  SummaryBackedChatAgent,
  [
    model: model,
    system: "You are an SRE assistant. Use remembered facts and retrieved context when relevant.",
    memory_store: memory_entries,
    retrieval_provider: retrieval_docs,
    llm_opts: llm_opts
  ],
  initial_message: "What do you remember about my deploy setup?"
)
```

## What To Notice

The model does not need to know how memory or retrieval works. The workflow
turns those sources into typed data, evaluates window pressure, and projects a
prompt bundle at the edge. That keeps the transcript truthful and makes derived
context replaceable.
